        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\n\t\t\t\t\t \n\n                 \t\n\n\n\t « All Events\n\n\t\n\tThis event has passed.\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\tJankura Lounge Exhibition: Quentin Harris\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\tJune 4, 2024 @ 10:00 am - June 28, 2024 @ 2:00 pm\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\nQuentin Harris has been practicing West Coast Native Art for over thirty years. Born Secwepemc, yet raised coastal, has resulted in Quentin finding his own style. He aspires to intersect First Nations art and culture with positive values and truth.\nAbout the Art: Frog is the messenger. He carries his important message far and wide – over land, to the other side of lakes, or to the deepest caves. There isn’t anywhere where frog won’t go. Frog’s message is simple:\n“Look at me – aren’t I a marvel? Can you see my green skin? Can you see my heart beat? Look around you – isn’t the world a beautiful place? This world didn’t happen by accident. The eagles circling high above the mountains. The whales singing in the depths of the ocean. Someone made everything that is good and righteous. Someone made it all with tremendous amounts of love. That same someone made you and me with infinite amounts of love. A love that wonders. A love that renews. A love that forgives. That someone has a name. Do you want to renew that relationship? Perhaps today? Can you see my heart beat?”\nFrog carries an important message. It is up to us how we receive it. We can greet his message with optimism, hope and open questions. Or we can throw away his message with pessimism, hopelessness and anger. You choose…\nViewings 10am-2pm Tuesday-Friday and before evening and weekend performances.\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\t Details \n\t\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tStart:\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t June 4, 2024 @ 10:00 am \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tEnd:\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t June 28, 2024 @ 2:00 pm \n\t\t\t\t