        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\n\t\t\t\t\t \n\n                 \t\n\n\n\t « All Events\n\n\t\n\tThis event has passed.\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\tArchipelago – Contemporary Art of the Salish Sea\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\tApril 22, 2023 @ 10:00 am - 4:00 pm\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t12 Artists. 6 Mediums. 3 Exhibitions. 2 Countries. 1 Sea. \nExhibition open daily from Saturday April 22 – Wednesday May 24 | 10am–4pm\nOpening Reception Friday April 21 | ArtSpring 5pm-7pm\nArtist Panel 1 Saturday April 22 | ArtSpring 10:30 am\nArtist Panel 2 Saturday April 22 |Mahon Hall 2:00 pm\nArtSpring is proud to present its first international visual art exhibition, Archipelago: Contemporary Art of the Salish Sea as part of a unique and important cultural exchange between two of North America’s most feted arts communities – the Southern Gulf Islands of British Columbia and the San Juan Islands of Washington State.\nFor this celebration of artistic life surrounding the Salish Sea, artists and their bodies of work will be moving between the islands. ArtSpring is thrilled to host and present six of the finest visual artists working in the San Juan Islands, exhibiting in Canada for the first time.\nDanielle Dean (photography)\nGlenn Hendrick (printmaking, painting)\nJoe Miller (oil painting, watercolour)\nRaVae Luckhart (oil painting, mixed media)\nRaven Skyriver (glass)\nTom Small (stone, sculpture).\nIn turn, Salt Spring Arts is presenting six of the finest visual artists working in the Southern Gulf Islands April 14-30, who will then be shown in September 22-December 4 in the San Juans.\nAnna Gustafson (installation)\nJane Kidd (textiles/tapestry)\nJoanna Rogers (textiles/found object)\nJohn Macdonald (painting)\nSam Montalbetti (photography)\nTemoseng, Chazz Elliott(sculpture/carvings)\nArchipelago is a collaboration with Salt Spring Arts (April 14-30 at Mahon Hall,) who will be exhibiting the Southern Gulf Island artists, and the San Juan Islands Museum of Art (September 22-December 4.)\nCurated by Richard Steel and Patrick McCallum of Salt Spring Island and Peter Lane of San Juan Islands.\n \n \n \n \n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\t Details \n\t\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tDate:\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t April 22, 2023 \n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tTime:\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t10:00 am - 4:00 pm\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\tEvent Categories: ArtSpring Presents, ArtSpring Presents 2022-2023, Gallery Exhibits & Events\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\n\n\n\tOrganizer\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tArtSpring Presents\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\tPhone\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t250.537.2102\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\tEmail\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\ttickets@artspring.ca\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\tView Organizer Website\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\n\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\n\t Venue \n\t\n\t\t\t\t ArtSpring – Gallery \n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n100 Jackson Avenue\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\tSalt Spring Island,\n\n\n\tV8K 2V8\n\n\tCanada\n\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t+ Google Map\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\tPhone\n\t\t\t\t\t 250.537.2102 \n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\n\n\n\t\n\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\tAdd to calendar\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\tGoogle Calendar\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\tiCalendar\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\tOutlook 365\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\tOutlook Live\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t \n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\t Details \n\t\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tDa