        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\n\t\t\t\t\t \n\n                 \t\n\n\n\t « All Events\n\n\t\n\tThis event has passed.\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\tARCHIPELAGO ARTIST PANEL 1\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\tApril 22, 2023 @ 10:30 am - 12:00 pm\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\nJoin us for a fascinating Archipelago Artist Panel 1 at 10:30am as three Southern Gulf Island and three San Juan Island artists discuss the inspirations and implications behind their work. Moderated by co-curators Richard Steel and Patrick McCallum, the conversation is expected to range from individual techniques to how living on the Salish Sea impacts their work to exploring if the Canadian-American border affects any commonalities or contrasts in this very special geo-political place.\nIf you are an art lover and want to join the conversation — this panel is a must attend.\nArtists on Panel 1 include:\nJoe Miller, John Macdonald, Sam Montalbetti, Danielle Dean, Glenn Hendrick, Anna Gustafson\nFor more information:Artist Panel 1 at ArtSpring at 10:30\nArtists on Panel 2 include:\nJane Kidd, Joanna Rogers, RaVae Lockhart, Raven Skyriver, Temoseng Chazz Elliott, Tom Small.\nArtist Panel 2 hosted at Mahon Hall at 2pm.\nFREE of CHARGE\n[Painting: Joe Miller Sea Plane 55 X 49” Oil on Linen]\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\t Details \n\t\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tDate:\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t April 22, 2023 \n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tTime:\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t10:30 am - 12:00 pm\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\tEvent Category: ArtSpring Presents\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tWebsite:\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t www.artspring.ca \n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\n\n\n\tOrganizer\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tArtSpring\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\tPhone\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t250.537.2102\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\tEmai