        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\n\t\t\t\t\t \n\n                 \t\n\n\n\t « All Events\n\n\t\n\tThis event has passed.\n\t\n\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\n\t\n\n\t\n\t\n\t\tEvent Series:\t\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tFull – Youth Art Enrichment Program\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\tFull – Youth Art Enrichment Program\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\tNovember 2, 2018 @ 10:00 am - 1:00 pm\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n \n \n \n \nYouth Art Enrichment Program\nOn Vincent van Gogh\nSERIES: Youth Programs\nThis program is now FULL. \nOctober 12, 19, 26, November 2, 2018\n10:00am-1:00pm\nFree\nRegister in-person at the ArtSpring Box Office, email tickets@artspring.ca, or by phone 250.537.2102.\nChildren ages 7 to 14 will explore the work and life of the Dutch Master painter Vincent Van Gogh and replicate his style through carving, texturizing and sculpting clay plaques, painting self-portraits with acrylics on canvas, sketching local landscapes using pen, ink and charcoal, and by creating 3D oil pastel paintings. Students will view sections of Loving Vincent (the world’s first fully painted feature film) to learn about Van Gogh’s life and his painting and sketching style. Facilitated by Tracy Harrison, a multimedia visual artist, arts educator, and Art Therapist \nGenerously sponsored by Country Grocer.\n \n \nGallery Show for Youth Art Enrichment Program\nNovember 2, 5, 6, 2018\nOpening Reception Nov 2 at 3:00pm – 4:30pm\nDaily Nov 5 & 6 at 10:00am – 4:00pm\nExhibit of artwork produced by the children participating in the Youth Art Enrichment Program.\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\t Details \n\t\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tDate:\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t November 2, 2018 \n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tTime:\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t10:00 am - 1:00 pm\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\tSeries: \n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tFull – Youth Art Enrichment Program\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t