        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\n\t\t\t\t\t \n\n                 \t\n\n\n\t « All Events\n\n\t\n\tThis event has passed.\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\tVETTA CHAMBER MUSIC: VIVALDI’S FOUR SEASONS & SEASONS OF THE SEA featuring Joan Blackman (violin)\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\tApril 27, 2016 @ 7:30 pm - 9:30 pm\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t-\n\t\t\t\t\t\t$5 – $28\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tViolinist Joan Blackman and Storyteller Rosemary Georgeson\nTo celebrate their 30th anniversary, Vancouver’s Vetta Chamber Players perform the Vivaldi’s ever popular Four Seasons and pair it with a work inspired by the sea and its seasons – a special commission composed by Vancouver’s own Jeffrey Ryan, in collaboration with Sahtu Dene and Coast Salish storyteller Rosemary Georgeson. Interspersed with the music, Georgeson will tell us stories around each season or time of year relating to her peoples’ life by and on the sea.\nThe performance features Salt Spring’s own violinist Joan Blackman, with Jennie Press and Carolyn Canfield Cole violins; Tawnya Popoff viola; Rebecca Wenham cello; Dylan Palmer bass; and Michael Jarvis harpsichord.\nProudly sponsored by Lyle & Susan Eide.\n*For more information about VETTA, visit their website and read the Vancouver Sun article about VETTA (published Sept. 2, 2015).\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\t Details \n\t\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tDate:\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t April 27, 2016 \n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tTime:\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t7:30 pm - 9:30 pm\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tCost:\n\t\t\t\t $5 – $28 \n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\tEvent Category: ArtSpring Presents\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\n\n\n\tOrganizer\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tArtSpring\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\tPhone\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t250.537.2102\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\tEm