    "https://schema.org/mainContentOfPage": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\n\t\t\t\t\t \n\n                 \t\n\n\n\t « All Events\n\n\t\n\tThis event has passed.\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\tSS FORUM’S 5th ANNIVERSARY FEATURING LAWRENCE MARTIN\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\tFebruary 13, 2016 @ 6:30 pm - 9:00 pm\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t-\n\t\t\t\t\t\t$15 – $20\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tThe Salt Spring Forum celebrates its 5th birthday by welcoming back the very first Forum speaker, Globe & Mail National Affairs Columnist and author Lawrence Martin. After a discussion in the theatre with Martin on The Undoing of Harperland: Where Trudeau Will Lead Canada, be sure to stay for a special reception in the gallery.\nLawrence Martin is the author of ten books and an Ottawa-based columnist for The Globe and Mail on public affairs. He served as the Globe’s bureau chief in Montreal, Washington and Moscow. Martin’s books include several critically-acclaimed national best-sellers: biographies of Jean Chretien as well as Lucien Bouchard, two volumes on Canada-U.S. relations, and a history of the Gorbachev government. Martin’s most recent book Harperland exposed the unprecedented degree of control that Stephen Harper exercised over Ottawa institutions as well as the anti-democratic nature of the Harper government.\n*Please note the earlier than usual 6:30 pm start time in the theatre. The gallery reception takes place at 8:00 pm.\n*The Salt Spring Forum thanks Garry Oaks Winery, Salt Spring Cheese, Hastings House, Harbour Air, and the Salt Spring Exchange for the generous support.\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\t Details \n\t\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tDate:\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t February 13, 2016 \n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tTime:\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t6:30 pm - 9:00 pm\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tCost:\n\t\t\t\t $15 – $20 \n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\tEvent Categories: Gallery 